"DPDA me har situation me sirf ek hi move hoti hai (no guessing). Isliye ye NPDA se weak hai. aⁿbⁿ DCFL hai par palindromes wwᴿ nahi, kyunki beech ka point guess karna padta hai.",
"A stack machine that cannot guess; it must decide each action from what it sees now.",
"{aⁿbⁿ} is accepted by a DPDA. {wcwᴿ} is DCFL (the marker c shows the middle). {wwᴿ} is CFL but not DCFL.",
["Determinism: |δ(q,a,X)|+|δ(q,ε,X)| ≤ 1.","Accepts by final state (empty-stack acceptance is weaker for DPDA).","DCFL ⊂ CFL (proper).","DCFLs are closed under complement but not under union or intersection.","DCFLs have unambiguous grammars; LR(k) grammars generate exactly DCFLs.","Compilers (parsers) use DPDA-like LR parsing."],
["Determinism condition.","DCFL vs CFL examples.","Complement closure."],
["Decide if a language is DCFL.","Design a DPDA.","Compare with NPDA."],
["Thinking all CFLs are DCFL.","Believing DPDA and NPDA are equivalent."],
